--   $0<\varepsilon\leq10^{-4}$, and
--   $0<y_1,y_2y_3\leq\varepsilon/k$.
--   Let $T=\tau_\downarrow(y)$, $o=\Psi_0(y,T)$ and $p=p_-(F_\downarrow(y))$.
--   Then $o=(-p_0,p_1,1,p_2)$ and
--   $$4\leq p_0,\quad k/2\leq p_0<k,\quad
--   0<p_1\leq\varepsilon/p_0,\quad0<p_2\leq\varepsilon,$$
--   $$p_1\leq y_1e^{-k/12},\quad p_2\leq y_2y_3,\quad
--   \sqrt{(p_0+1)^2+1}=\mathfrak r(o).$$
--   The normalized chart clock is positive at $T$, the connection is valid,
--   $T_-$ and $P_-$ are $C^2$ at $p$, and
--   $P_-(p)=\Psi_0(y,T+T_-(p))$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/l46430640-del/ERA-STATISTICS-FORMAL/blob/d74c241819f896ab8d050b21ace80c8e90eabd9e/BianchiIX/Dynamics/PartialCoreDownwardConnection.lean#L29-L102

